WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:18.180
Happy birthday dear mom. Happy birthday to you.

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:20.053
Good morning, John. It's Friday, March 16th.

00:00:20.053 --> 00:00:21.750
Today is an important day for

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:23.670
Brotherhood 2.0 for more than

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:26.099
one reason. A significant importance to

00:00:26.099 --> 00:00:28.890
Brotherhood 2.0 is ZeFrank, who

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:32.040
likely inspired a lot of what

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:34.079
we're doing here. Maybe even a little bit

00:00:34.079 --> 00:00:36.149
more than we realized sometimes.

00:00:36.149 --> 00:00:38.070
ZeFrank has made a hilarious video every

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:39.870
weekday for the past year. By doing this

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:41.370
he has garnered international attention

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:43.469
in publication in the New York Times and

00:00:43.469 --> 00:00:45.899
a viewership of hundreds of thousands. We

00:00:45.899 --> 00:00:47.520
would like to be as popular as ZeFrank

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.379
but we will never be. Because we aren't

00:00:49.379 --> 00:00:51.780
anywhere near as cool as ZeFrank. But

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:53.789
starting today, that doesn't matter

00:00:53.789 --> 00:00:56.520
anymore. ZeFrank viewers won't be able

00:00:56.520 --> 00:01:01.829
to watch ZeFrank anymore. Thus, I think ZeFrank viewers maybe should come

00:01:01.829 --> 00:01:04.170
check out the Brotherhood. Welcomes

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:07.500
ZeFrank viewers. Any of you out there? Isn't

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.939
it gonna be a horrible life without

00:01:08.939 --> 00:01:11.130
having ZeFrank to procrastinate with?

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:14.880
You can procrastinate with us. I mean we

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:18.270
blink. ZeFrank doesn't blink. We write

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:22.740
songs though but they're not as good as ZeFrank songs. And we have projects that

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:24.270
our viewers can participate in with us.

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:26.520
But none of them are anywhere near as

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:28.380
cool as making the entire world of

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:30.299
sandwich. Second reason that this is a

00:01:30.299 --> 00:01:31.860
very important day for Brotherhood 2.0

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:33.750
is because there is only one

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:35.880
person who is vital to the creation of

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:38.520
the Brotherhood and that is our mom.

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:40.890
Actually today isn't mom's birthday.

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:42.720
Tomorrow is mom's birthday but tomorrow,

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:44.520
it's Saturday. There won't be

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:47.880
any Brotherhood 2.0 in tomorrow.

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:49.380
So I'm taking the opportunity to

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:51.240
celebrate mom's birthday a day early on

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:53.189
Brotherhood 2.0. Now there

00:01:53.189 --> 00:01:54.960
really is no one who's more important

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:56.820
Brotherhood 2.0 than our mom. I

00:01:56.820 --> 00:02:00.299
mean we both came out of her and I

00:02:00.299 --> 00:02:03.210
really and truly want to thank her for

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:05.250
that. I know it must not have been very

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:08.429
fun. I have a pretty big head and I guess

00:02:08.429 --> 00:02:09.509
it didn't really get all that much

00:02:09.509 --> 00:02:12.629
easier for you. I mean that first day was

00:02:12.629 --> 00:02:13.500
bad

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:14.910
and then there were probably some bad

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:17.310
days pretty soon after that. And I know there

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:20.040
were some bad days a few years after

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:22.590
that and then high school was like, all

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:24.870
bad days and then I'm at the college and

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:27.720
I just never called you. Oh. Happy

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:30.450
birthday mom. Having kids kind of sucks.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:32.280
But I hope you know that they appreciate

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:34.350
you. Your support has been vital. This

00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:36.000
might seem a little bit stupid or

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.970
callous or maybe even inhuman but I

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:40.380
think you should be able to own stock in

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:43.410
people. So for example when a child is

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:45.690
born, the parents have a minority stake

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:49.050
in the interests of the child whereas

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:51.390
the child would own a full 51% of itself,

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:53.580
the parents would only own 49. The child

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:55.290
could never sell its majority stake but

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:57.209
the parents could sell their minority

00:02:57.209 --> 00:02:59.610
stake to different people. Like when the

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:01.170
kid goes off to college, the parents

00:03:01.170 --> 00:03:02.700
could sell like ten percent of the kid

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:04.230
to the college and that way the college

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:05.880
can get something back from the kid for

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:07.440
what it gives to the kid. And then later

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:09.090
the kid might want to buy some of his

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:11.010
stock back from you. So he'll have more

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:12.690
than a 51-percent stake in his self.

00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:14.790
Knowing my mom, she'd probably just give

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:16.620
me that forty-nine percent and I don't a

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:18.660
hundred percent of myself. But it seems

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:19.980
somehow wrong that people can put so

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:21.810
much energy into a person and then that

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:23.220
person gets to take all that energy and

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:24.750
do whatever they want with it. Mom,

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:26.519
shouldn't you be getting something back?

00:03:26.519 --> 00:03:28.380
You invested a lot of time and effort

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:31.590
and worry and discomfort in me. And I

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:32.940
feel bad that I just have all that stuff

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:35.040
that you gave me and I can do whatever I

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:36.450
want with it. I guess what I'm trying to

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:39.630
say is moms are great and they do it all

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:44.660
for nothing. I'll see you on Monday.

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:48.500
And if the world were a sandwich, we

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:54.790
could all be one sandwich.

